      {
        "id": "u8",
        "parent": "x59",
        "stage": "frontend",
        "catalog_id": "F-8",
        "delta": "set inner-loop unroll_list. The values are PARALLEL BLOCK SIZES in descending priority order, not unroll counts: [8,4,2,1] asks for 8 blocks in parallel and falls back through 4, 2, 1. Innermost pypto.loop only (OL49), and no value above that loop's trip count. A bigger loop wants a longer list -- [8,4,2,1] is the adaptable default, [128,64,16,8,1] suits large ones, and [128,64,16,4,1] measured 3.3x to 8.9x on six GroupedMatmulSwigluQuant cases, bit-exact. Each value costs one compilation path (OL56), so length is paid in wall clock. Pairs with F-7: chunk the outer axis for task granularity, then unroll the inner one for parallelism -- neither alone reaches what the two do together.",
