        "stage": "frontend",
        "delta": "Split the nope head-axis (128) into G groups inside M2 so the q_nope_raw view literal drops below the 192KB UB budget and the static feasibility gate stops rejecting every candidate. Concretely: replace `q_nope_raw = pypto.view(q_reshape,[8,128,128],[0,0,0])` (256KB) with a Python `for g in range(4)` that views `pypto.view(q_reshape,[8,32,128],[0,g*32,0])` (64KB), slices the batch weight per group via `pypto.view(w_uk,[32,128,512],[g*32,0,0])`, runs the existing permute->matmul->permute on each group, and assembles into q_nope_out at [bs_offset,g*32,0] -- exactly mirroring the head split already in pypto_stage_rope_3d. This shrinks the max GM-window view from 256KB to ~112KB (x_tile) and raises task count (4 groups).",
        "V": 0.9,
        "prior_gain": 0.9,
        "tried": 0,
        "pruned_on": "ea109294b361"
      },
      {
        "id": "u60",
        "parent": "x59",
        "stage": "swimlane",
        "delta": "overlap the data-independent nope (cube matmul) and rope (vector rope_3d) branches so they run concurrently instead of as a serial cube-then-vector recurrence: issue the two branches so the vector pipe's rope_3d work fills the bubble while the cube pipe runs the q_nope matmuls (and vice versa). Both branches are independent until the final combine/concat, so there is no data dependency forcing serialization. Targets the 20.49% vector utilisation and the 79.02% predecessor stall directly.",
        "V": 0.8,
        "prior_gain": 0.9,
        "tried": 0
      }
